  "enhanced_information": "When centrifuging human peripheral blood in a density gradient in Ficoll, mononuclear cells float on the Ficoll due to their lower density compared to granulocytes and erythrocytes. Monocytes may also float on the Ficoll layer, but some may remain in the background. Lymphocytes may remain in the background due to their density relative to other blood components. Erythrocytes float on the Ficoll layer due to their higher density. Evidence supports interactions between monocytes and erythrocytes, granulocytes, and mononuclear cells."
